:: Carter Hero Award Part 7 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 50>>
You’re not sure when you fell asleep, but you awaken sometime later still in the treehouse. It feels strangely warm and open your eyes to see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> lying next to you under the covers. <span style="color:Yellow">Wait, under the covers?</span> You sit up to find that a pillow had been placed under your head and a blanket draped over the two of you. <span style="color:Pink">Someone had come up while you two were sleeping and brought them out here to keep you warm.</span> You stretch your arms up and glance outside, it’s late, the sun already has gone down. You’d guess you were asleep for a few hours at least and wonder what time it is. <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Eyes: "Tired",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Everyday",
                Eyes: "Tired",
                Blush: 1,
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Huh?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> mumbles as he wakes up, sitting up groggily and rubbing his eyes, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$CarterNickname</span>? What are-?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> pauses, looking around the space and down at the blanket, smiling. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh, guess we fell asleep. Sorry, I have a bad habit of that.”</span> He laughs, his normal cheerful energy returning <span style="color:Yellow">though you can still see some dried wet marks on his cheeks as he stands up.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thankfully dad normally checks on me and brings out blankets, so I don’t catch a cold. He used to carry me down to bed, but that got a little harder once I got older.”</span> <br>
<br>
You and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> clean up a little, not planning to spend the entire night in his treehouse. As you do, you want to say something, see if he’s really alright after what happened earlier. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> must be able to tell what you are thinking, as he smiles. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m fine, really. Like I said I… I lost my head for a second. But it was nice to talk about it with you, I… I don’t really talk about it… ever, really. So, thanks.”</span> He smiles, seeming genuinely happy. <span style="color:Yellow">Even if it’s hard to accept, he seems fine now.</span> It is as you two are finishing up that a voice calls down from below. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>? Are you guys awake?”</span> It’s his dad, his voice still a little nervous. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah! Sorry, we didn’t mean to fall asleep, guess I was pretty tired from… everything.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> pauses briefly before finishing his sentence, <span style="color:Yellow">no doubt reminded of what happened and choosing not to directly mention the award ceremony. He dropped his award when he ran out here, you recall seeing it broken. You wonder if <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> knows what happened to it.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It- it’s fine.”</span> His dad responds from the porch, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>’s dad is here to pick him up. It’s getting late, so he should probably be heading home.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Ah, dang.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> sighs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I was hoping we’d have time for pizza and at least one episode! Sorry about that. Hey, maybe we could have a do-over sometime? Maybe during a sleepover? Pizza and movies! Maybe we could get a TV hooked up out here, wouldn’t that be cool?”</span> While worried about <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, you don’t want to spoil his good mood, so you smile and nod, saying you’d love that. If <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> doesn’t want to talk right now, you won’t force it, but as you both begin to climb down, <span style="color:Yellow">you tell <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> that you’ll always be ready to listen, if he wants to talk.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thanks. Really, it means a lot.”</span> <span style="color:Pink">He smiles as you both reach the bottom, pausing for a moment before jumping in for a tight hug.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m really glad I met you. You’re a good friend.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Next time, maybe I’ll tell you about <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says quietly, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“The real <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>.”</span> <br>
<br>
You smile at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> as you both walk inside. He yawns and rubs his eyes, still tired. You look at the kitchen, <span style="color:Yellow">no sign of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s broken award.</span> They must have picked it up; you wonder when <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> will find out it broke and feel your chest tighten as you think about that. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> gives you one last smile before heading to his room, looking ready for a proper sleep. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:Yellow">As you walk to the door with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s dad, you want to say something, but what?</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
    <<link "Tell him Carter’s a good kid<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        You stop at the door, turning to his dad and say that Carter is a good kid, a great kid even. He’s friendly and kind and selfless and… <span style="color:Yellow">and he deserves to be seen for the good person he is. His dad looks at you with pained eyes, then sighs.</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                        Eyes: "Mad",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You’re right, he’s the best kid. He’s a lot braver than me.”</span> He pauses, knowing everything you’re saying is right and feeling shame at his own actions, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thank you, for being his friend. I’m really glad he has you.”</span> As he opens the door and you walk outside where <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> is waiting, you turn back briefly. <span style="color:Yellow">From here you can see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>’s room, or what they pretend to be his room, open just a crack. A shadow of someone inside, sitting on the bed.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hey kiddo.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Dad</span> says with a smile, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hope you had fun. Ready to go?”</span> <br>
        <<include"Carter Hero Award Part 7 End Code">>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
    <<link "Tell him he needs to do better<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        You stop at the door, turning to his dad with a determined expression and say what’s on your mind, blunt and frank. <span style="color:Yellow">He needs to do better, they all do, for <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> is the only thing holding them together, but he’s just a kid. He doesn’t deserve this, he deserves better. His dad looks at you with pained eyes, then sighs.</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                        Eyes: "Mad",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You’re right. He deserves… so much better.”</span> He pauses, shame in his blank eyes, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’ve been saying I’ll try my best for years, maybe I should stop trying and start doing.”</span> He seems to be mostly talking to himself, but at the very least it may be a step in the right direction. As he opens the door and you walk outside where <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> is waiting, you turn back briefly. <span style="color:Yellow">From here you can see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>’s room, or what they pretend to be his room, open just a crack. A shadow of someone inside, sitting on the bed.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hey kiddo.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Dad</span> says with a smile, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hope you had fun. Ready to go?”</span> <br>
        <<include"Carter Hero Award Part 7 End Code">>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
    <<link "Tell him nothing<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        You want to say something, but don’t. Whether you’re afraid of getting involve, think it isn’t your place, or just don’t want to say what this man has to already know, <span style="color:Yellow">you just look at him. Even without words, your look says everything you need to say. He looks at you with pained eyes, before sighing.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thanks… for being his friend. I’m… really glad he has you.”</span> <br>
        <br>
        As he opens the door and you walk outside where <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> is waiting, you turn back briefly. <span style="color:Yellow">From here you can see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>’s room, or what they pretend to be his room, open just a crack. A shadow of someone inside, sitting on the bed.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hey kiddo.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Dad</span> says with a smile, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hope you had fun. Ready to go?”</span> <br>
        <<include"Carter Hero Award Part 7 End Code">>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
</div>

